<?xml version="1.0"?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
	<EntityComponents>

<!-- Airfield ownership state machine - UNIVERSAL, shared by every secondary airfield
     installation (not per-installation). Checks all 3 anchors per faction (Gray: La Spezia/
     Tripoli/Rome, Green: Toulon/Oran/Alexandria) via OR ([AllowAnyTrueBoolean:true]) rather
     than a hand-picked "nearest anchors" subset per airfield - functionally identical for any
     given airfield (the far anchors just never go true, since a real airfield is never inside
     a tier-1 zone on the other side of the map), but means a brand new airfield anywhere only
     needs its own SpawnGroup + Prefab + SpawnConditions pointing at these SAME Behaviors -
     zero new trigger/condition/behavior authoring per airfield.

     Only ONE boolean per anchor (In<Faction>_<Anchor>), not two - confirmed directly from
     current MES source (ConditionReferenceProfile.cs) that CheckFalseBooleans/FalseBooleans/
     AllowAnyFalseBoolean exist alongside the true-boolean equivalents, so "not in territory"
     is checked by requiring all 3 anchor booleans FALSE rather than needing a second, redundant
     "Out" boolean per anchor. Two TRIGGERS per anchor (enter/exit) are still required, though
     - RivalAI has no if/else within a single Trigger, so InsideActiveZone/OutsideActiveZone
     have to be separate Trigger objects even though they are logical complements.

     ONE always-on Behavior (WW2-Behavior-Airfield). MES's [SwitchToBehavior] cannot be used:
     ChangeBehavior re-registers the Remote Control, but BehaviorManager.RegisterBehaviorFromRemoteControl
     returns early for any Remote Control already in RegisteredRemoteBlocks (never cleared), so the new
     Behavior never starts. Instead the state lives in which triggers are enabled: the Gray/Green decision
     triggers and every feature trigger (store, offense, cargo request, reputation, defence, bots) start
     [UseTrigger:false], and each flip action enables the new state's set and disables the old one
     (the GVK Supply Depot pattern).

     Territory check: confirmed via current MES source (TriggerChecks.cs) that
     [Type:InsideActiveZone]/[OutsideActiveZone] + [ZoneName:...] calls
     ZoneManager.InsideZoneWithName() - real and working (a GVK reference mod comment calling
     this buggy appears to be from an older MES version).

     ZONE NAMES: ZoneManager.InsideZoneWithName() compares [ZoneName:] against the zone's
     PublicName (confirmed from MES source), NOT its profile SubtypeId - so these must be
     {Anchor}_Zone (the PublicName in Territory-Zones.sbc), not WW2-Territory-Zone-{Anchor}.
     (This file previously used SubtypeId-style names, which could never match.)

     Territory-Zones.sbc now has ONE resizable zone per anchor (5km-35km, grown/shrunk by
     Triggers-Zone-Change.sbc), so these triggers follow the anchor's CURRENT territory
     radius automatically - no need to check separate per-tier zones. -->

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Trigger-Airfield-ZoneCheckIn-Gray-LaSpezia</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>
			[RivalAI Trigger]
			[UseTrigger:true]
			[Type:InsideActiveZone]
			[ZoneName:LaSpezia_Zone]
			[MinCooldownMs:5000]
			[MaxCooldownMs:5001]
			[StartsReady:true]
			[MaxActions:-1]
			[Actions:WW2-Action-Airfield-ZoneCheckIn-Gray-LaSpezia]
			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Action-Airfield-ZoneCheckIn-Gray-LaSpezia</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>
			[RivalAI Action]
			[SetBooleansTrue:true]
			[SetBooleansTrue:InGray_LaSpezia]
			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Trigger-Airfield-ZoneCheckOut-Gray-LaSpezia</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>
			[RivalAI Trigger]
			[UseTrigger:true]
			[Type:OutsideActiveZone]
			[ZoneName:LaSpezia_Zone]
			[MinCooldownMs:5000]
			[MaxCooldownMs:5001]
			[StartsReady:true]
			[MaxActions:-1]
			[Actions:WW2-Action-Airfield-ZoneCheckOut-Gray-LaSpezia]
			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
